/*
 * H96 Max 3518D TV box (PCB silkscreen 3518_DG_ZX_V01) — Rockchip RK3518, RK3528 family.
 *
 * A stick-form sibling of the 3518_ZX_V01 board, from the same vendor tree. Most of what
 * differs is hardware this PCB does not have, switched off rather than described.
 * The console also differs: the 3518_ZX_V01 frees ff9f0000 for ttyS0, while this box keeps the
 * vendor's fiq-debugger on it and boots with console=ttyFIQ0, so uart0 stays disabled
 * and fiq-debugger stays enabled — neither is a departure here.
 *
 * The vendor derived this box from Rockchip's EVB1 DDR4 V10 reference design and its
 * compatible still says so, so this includes that board and overrides what differs.
 *
 * Checked against the box's own factory device tree, carved from its eMMC: this file
 * compiles to a tree content-identical to that blob plus the changes below. The
 * overrides that follow are the box's own hardware, and carry no reasons because the
 * blob carries none; these are the deliberate departures from it.
 *
 *   compatible         board name first, as the Seekwave driver builds its firmware
 *                      filenames from it and this box's NV and RF calibration differ
 *                      from the ZX's; rk3528a last, as rkmpp has no rk3518 entry and
 *                      cannot otherwise find the VPU. The vendor bootloader rewrote
 *                      the SoC compatible to rk3528a at boot; ours does not, so the
 *                      append is load-bearing here rather than cosmetic.
 *   model              name the box, keeping the vendor string
 *   reboot-mode        mode-maskrom added, so `reboot maskrom` from the OS reaches the
 *                      BootROM; the factory SPL reads the register on the way up
 *   gpu@ff700000       interrupt-names and clocks in the form mainline lima expects,
 *                      not the vendor Mali blob's
 *   vop@ff840000       esmart_lb_mode 03 -> 02, giving Esmart0 a 4K line buffer. At 03
 *                      every Esmart window gets 2K, so a 3840-wide mode fetches half a
 *                      line and the rest is whatever the buffer held
 *   watchdog@ffac0000  enabled, for systemd's RuntimeWatchdogSec
 *   leds               power/standby labels, renamed from the vendor's work-green and
 *                      work-red
 *   absent hardware    disabled, none of it fitted on this PCB: mmc@ffc30000 (no
 *                      microSD), ethernet@ffbd0000, tve@ff880000 (no AV jack),
 *                      spdif@ffbc0000 and acodec@ffe10000 with their sound cards,
 *                      spi@ffc00000, and pwm@ffa90030 (no IR receiver fitted, so the
 *                      remote is BLE-only here)
 *   chosen             dropped; u-boot supplies bootargs, and the vendor string names
 *                      ttyFIQ0
 */
